// Adds the coarse correction back onto the fine pressure field.
//
// Piecewise constant: one value per tile, added to all 512 of its cells. That
// leaves a jump at every tile face, which is high frequency and therefore exactly
// what the block sweep that follows removes — the division of labour a two-level
// method is made of. It is also why the coarse correction is always followed by
// smoothing and never comes last.
//
// In place on press_src rather than through the ping-pong: a tile writes only its
// own cells, so no workgroup reads what another is writing.

void main() {
	ivec3 c = cell_coord();
	if (coarse_idx[gl_WorkGroupID.x] != COARSE_INTERIOR || out_of_grid(c)) {
		return;
	}
	store_press_src(c, load_press_src(c) + coarse_val[COARSE_P_BASE + gl_WorkGroupID.x]);
}
